The caravan was led 
by Islam Bai, Turdu Bai, Khodai Kullu, and two Lop-men ; 
and Chernoff was commissioned to escort them to the mountains.

They sat outside their cabin and talked ; 
they circled around the ferry-boat in their canoes; they rowed 
to shore and shot wild-duck in the quiet angles of the stream ; 
and when their day’s work was done they amused themselves 
with fishing.

